# The build context is the repository root, but the Dockerfile only ever COPYs
# app/pyproject.toml, app/uv.lock and app/app/. Everything else is excluded so
# the context stays small and unrelated edits do not bust the dependency layer.
# Patterns are **-prefixed because the sources live one level down, under app/.

# app/.venv alone is ~190 MB / 9,000+ files — without this line every build
# ships all of it to the Docker daemon.
**/.venv

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Stale bytecode must never reach the image; the venv is byte-compiled at build
# time by UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE instead.
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

**/tests/
**/scripts/
**/*.md

.env
**/.env.*

Makefile
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
k8s/
.github/
*.log
